{{also|mjölk|mjǫlk|mjølk}}
==Faroese==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|fo}} {{m|non|mjǫlk}}, {{m|non|mjolk}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|fo}} {{m|gem-pro|*meluks}}, cognate with Danish {{m|da|mælk}}, Swedish {{m|sv|mjölk}}, English {{m|en|milk}}. Ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|fo}} {{m|ine-pro|*h₂melǵ-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[mjœl̥k]|lang=fo}}, ''[[Suðuroy]]:'' {{IPA|[mjʏl̥k]|lang=fo}}

===Noun===
{{fo-noun|f|mjólkar|-}}

# [[milk]]

====Declension====
{{fo-decl-noun-f2-s|mjólk}}
Note the lack of i-mutation in the genitive (from *melukiz ). Although the form would suggest a mutated **''mýlkur'', ''-jó-'' is not the original vowel (from *-eu-, as in {{m|fo|tjóð}} ), but a product of a double vowel change, first fracture: meluk- > mjǫlk, and then lengthening: o/ǫ > ó before lk. Also, the ability of the -iz to effect an i-mutation on the first vowel is reduced by the intermediate -u-.

