{{wikipedia|lang=is}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|mjǫlk}}, {{m|non|mjolk}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*meluks}}, cognate with Danish {{m|da|mælk}}, Swedish {{m|sv|mjölk}}, English {{m|en|milk}}. Ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{m|ine-pro|*h₂melǵ-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/mjoul̥k/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|oul̥k|lang=is}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|f|mjólkur|-}}

# [[milk]]
# any liquid resembling [[milk]], as the liquid within a coconut (e.g. [[kókosmjólk]]), the juice or sap of certain plants (''e.g.'' [[fíflamjólk]]), or various pharmaceutical preparations
# {{lb|is|rare}} [[milt]] from a [[fish]]

====Declension====
{{is-decl-noun-f-s3|m|jól|k|ur=ur|pl=-}}
Note the lack of i-mutation in the genitive (from *melukiz ). Although the form would suggest a mutated **''mýlkur'', ''-jó-'' is not the original vowel (from *-eu-, as in {{m|is|þjóð}} ), but a product of a double vowel change, first fracture: meluk- > mjǫlk, and then lengthening: o/ǫ > ó before lk. Also, the ability of the -iz to effect an i-mutation on the first vowel is reduced by the intermediate -u-.

